==Icelandic==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|is|áttján}} {{qualifier|archaic}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{m|non|átján}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{m|gem-pro|*ahtōutehun}}. Cognate with the Swedish {{m|sv|arton}}, Danish {{m|da|atten}}, English {{m|en|eighteen}} and German {{m|de|achtzehn}}.

===Numeral===
'''átján'''

# '''[[eighteen]]'''; the cardinal number after [[sautján#Icelandic|sautján]] and before [[nítján#Icelandic|nítján]].

====Derived terms====
* {{l|is|einn af átján}}
* {{l|is|nú tekur átján yfir}}, {{l|is|nú kastar átján yfir}}
* {{l|is|sjá upp á átján augum}}

====Related terms====
* (''ordinal form'') [[átjándi]] {{g|m}}, [[átjánda]] {{g|f|n}}

